:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=NETSTAT.Work with TCP/IP Network Sts (NETSTAT)
:P.The Work with TCP/IP Network Sts (NETSTAT) command works with the
network status&colon. interfaces, routes, connections.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETSTAT/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT, *IFC, *RTE, *CNN, *IFC6, *RTE6, *CNN6,
*STATUS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PING.Verify TCP/IP Connection (PING)
:P.Use the Verify TCP/IP Connection (PING) command to ICMP echo requests
to a remote system, from the job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
:P.The remote system, by host name or internet address.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*INTNETADR:EPK.
:PD.The internet address given in INTNETADR.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/INTNETADR'.Remote internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/ADRVERFMT'.Address version format (ADRVERFMT)
:P.The address version format for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IP4, *IP6.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/MSGMODE'.Message mode (MSGMODE)
:P.The message mode for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Response message detail
:P.Also accepted&colon. *VERBOSE, *QUIET.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Summary, if response errors
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COMP, *ESCAPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/PKTLEN'.Packet length (in bytes) (PKTLEN)
:P.The packet length (in bytes) for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 8 to 65500.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 256 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/NBRPKT'.Number of packets (NBRPKT)
:P.The number of packets for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 5 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/WAITTIME'.Wait time (in seconds) (WAITTIME)
:P.How many seconds the command waits for a response.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 120.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/LCLINTNETA'.Local internet address (LCLINTNETA)
:P.The local internet address for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/TOS'.Type of service (TOS)
:P.The type of service for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MINDELAY, *MAXTHRPUT, *MAXRLB, *MINCOST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PING/IPTTL'.IP time to live (hop limit) (IPTTL)
:P.The IP time to live (hop limit) for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TRACEROUTE.Trace TCP/IP Route (TRACEROUTE)
:P.The Trace TCP/IP Route (TRACEROUTE) command works with the routers on
the way to a remote system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
:P.The remote system, by host name or internet address.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/RANGE'.Range of hops to probe (RANGE)
:P.The range of hops to probe for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting probe TTL (hop limit)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Maximum probe TTL (hop limit)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/PROBES'.Probes sent per hop (PROBES)
:P.The probes sent per hop for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 64.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 3 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/WAITTIME'.Response wait time (WAITTIME)
:P.How many seconds the command waits for a response.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 120.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 3 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/PKTLEN'.Packet length (in bytes) (PKTLEN)
:P.The packet length (in bytes) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 40 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 40 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *VERBOSE, *DTAQ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/DTAQ'.Data queue (DTAQ)
:P.The data queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/ADRVERFMT'.Address version format (ADRVERFMT)
:P.The address version format for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IP4, *IP6.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/LCLINTNETA'.Source IP address (LCLINTNETA)
:P.The source IP address for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/RMTPORT'.Base remote port (RMTPORT)
:P.The base remote port for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 33434 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/NAMELOOKUP'.Lookup host names (NAMELOOKUP)
:P.Whether to lookup host names.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/PROBEPCL'.Probing protocol (PROBEPCL)
:P.The probing protocol for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ICMP:EPK.
:PD.ICMP.
:PT.:PK.*UDP:EPK.
:PD.UDP.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRACEROUTE/FRAGMENT'.Allow fragmentation (FRAGMENT)
:P.The allow fragmentation for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TCPA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TRCTCPRTE.Trace TCP/IP Route (TRCTCPRTE)
:P.Use the Trace TCP/IP Route (TRCTCPRTE) command to TRACEROUTE under
its other name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCTCPRTE/RMTSYS'.Remote system (RMTSYS)
